From: Carl Andersson <carl.andersson@dynamist.se>
Subject: [PATCH] virtio/fs: keep the guest's cache of a read-only share

libkrun answers every open with the Auto cache policy, which never sets
FOPEN_KEEP_CACHE, and the C API has no way to choose another. So the
guest drops its cache of a file each time any process opens it. On a
DAX mount that also drops the mappings of running processes, and since
Linux 6.15 those processes then get SIGBUS (smol-machines/smolvm#1741).

vivarium shares the host's /nix/store read-only, and nothing changes a
store path once it exists, so a guest's cache of it never goes stale.
A read-only share now uses the Always policy, as virtiofsd's
--cache=always does. The trap: a host that changes files below a
read-only share has its guest read the old contents until a lookup
sees the new attributes.
---
--- a/src/devices/src/virtio/fs/device.rs
+++ b/src/devices/src/virtio/fs/device.rs
@@ -88,6 +88,11 @@
             root_dir,
             semantics,
             attr_timeout,
+            cache_policy: if read_only {
+                passthrough::CachePolicy::Always
+            } else {
+                Default::default()
+            },
             ..Default::default()
         });

